# `test/line-endings.test.ts` detects a carriage return that has already been
# committed. This is what stops one arriving: `text=auto` normalises on the way
# into the object store, and `eol=lf` checks every text file out with LF on
# every platform, so a clone on Windows cannot reintroduce what the test would
# then have to catch. A guard that only reports is a guard that reports the same
# thing every time somebody clones.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Both OFL texts are redistributed byte-for-byte as their upstreams publish
# them, verified against the JetBrains Mono v2.304 release and against
# `ofl/majormonodisplay/OFL.txt` in google/fonts. The latter is published with
# CRLF terminators, so `-text` tells git to convert neither file in either
# direction — the alternative is a licence this repository did not write being
# silently rewritten to suit a house style. The line-ending test reads this same
# attribute rather than keeping its own list, so exempting a file here is the
# only place the exemption has to be stated.
fonts/*-OFL.txt -text

# The two subset faces are compressed binary. Naming them saves git sniffing
# content to reach the same conclusion, and keeps a diff from ever being
# attempted against bytes no reader can use.
*.woff2 binary
